Avoid a bogus GCC 16 -Wstringop-overflow error in Boost.MultiIndex.

GCC isolates an impossible path where the bucket array has SIZE_MAX buckets
and turns the loop into an oversized memset. With x<y the loop does not run on
that path. Both forms visit the same buckets on every possible path.

Remove once GCC or Boost fixes this.
Report: https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=129070

--- a/boost/multi_index/detail/bucket_array.hpp
+++ b/boost/multi_index/detail/bucket_array.hpp
@@ -162,7 +162,7 @@ public:
 
   void clear(pointer end_)
   {
-    for(base_pointer x=begin(),y=end();x!=y;++x)x->prior()=pointer(0);
+    for(base_pointer x=begin(),y=end();x<y;++x)x->prior()=pointer(0);
     end()->prior()=end_->prior()=end_;
     end_->next()=end();
  }
